tags: descendant-depth

A limit of the node: the most levels below one account that the node looks through to find a descendant by its instance_ref.

The value is an integer in levels. Example: 8. The node does not find a descendant deeper than the value: it answers as for an account that is not below.

The limit has no scope.

An absent limit is not a promise of no limit. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=limit
name=descendant-depth
per=one lookup of a descendant by its instance_ref (GetBalanceStatement, ServiceTunnel)
rule=The node does not find a descendant deeper than the value: it answers as for an account that is not below.
scope=none
unit=levels
